                          "text":  "Most Mars explorers look around. I was sent to listen. I landed on November 26, 2018, on a plain so flat and plain that my team happily called it the biggest parking lot on Mars. I did not need a view. I needed quiet.\n\nWith my arm I lifted my seismometer off my deck and set it gently on the ground, then covered it with a dome to keep the wind out. Then I waited. On April 6, 2019, I felt a faint tremble. A marsquake. The first one anyone had ever caught.",
